lipLoaderAny", "models": [{"name": "qwen3vl_32b_minimax_h3_int8_convrot.safetensors", "url": "https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3/resolve/main/text_encoders/qwen3vl_32b_minimax_h3_int8_convrot.safetensors", "directory": "text_encoders"}]}, "widgets_values": ["MiniMax-H3-encoder-Q4_K_M.gguf", "minimax"]}, {"id": 129, "type": "RandomNoise", "pos": [-287.2820394000002, 4938.228438999999], "size": [360, 90], "flags": {}, "order": 5, "mode": 0, "inputs": [], "outputs": [{"name": "NOISE", "type": "NOISE", "links": [253]}], "title": "Seed", "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.30.0", "Node name for S&R": "RandomNoise"}, "widgets_values": [157368968253448, "randomize"]}, {"id": 132, "type": "PrimitiveFloat", "pos": [-1477.0718, 5810.966699999998], "size": [270, 70], "flags": {}, "order": 6, "mode": 0, "inputs": [], "outputs": [{"name": "FLOAT", "type": "FLOAT", "links": [261]}], "title": "Float (Duration)", "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.30.0", "Node name for S&R": "PrimitiveFloat"}, "widgets_values": [5], "color": "#322", "bgcolor": "#533"}, {"id": 137, "type": "LoadImage", "pos": [-927.0718, 5610.966699999998], "size": [290, 330], "flags": {}, "order": 7, "mode": 0, "inputs": [], "outputs": [{"name": "IMAGE", "type": "IMAGE", "links": [278]}, {"name": "MASK", "type": "MASK", "links": null}], "title": "Reference image 1  ->  <Picture 1>", "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.30.0", "Node name for S&R": "LoadImage"}, "widgets_values": ["example.png", "image"]}, {"id": 138, "type": "PrimitiveStringMultiline", "pos": [-1477.0718, 5980.966699999998], "size": [370, 390], "flags": {}, "order": 8, "mode": 0, "inputs": [], "outputs": [{"name": "STRING", "type": "STRING", "links": [279]}], "title": "Input Text (Prompt)", "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.30.0", "Node name for S&R": "PrimitiveStringMultiline"}, "widgets_values": ["Bold comic-book ink style, heavy linework, red and blue-black palette, night city. Use <Picture 2> and <Picture 1> as reference frames and <Audio 1> exactly as it is.\nCUT 1: top-down view of the little boy superhero on the rooftop \u2014 red cape fluttering in the wind, hands planted on his hips, freckles and a cocky grin as he looks straight up into the camera. The camera slowly descends toward him as he delivers his line \u2014 as he speaks, comic-book graphic overlay text word by word in sync with his voice: \"GET READY TO\" - \"MEET\" \u2014 \"YOUR\" \u2014 \"MAKER\" \u2014 huge jagged comic lettering, white with heavy black outlines and red drop shadows, tilted at scrappy angles, until the three words hang stacked in the air above him between his face and the lens.\nTRANSITION: a violent WHIP PAN off the rooftop that SMEARS the floating words away with it, motion-streaked \u2014\nCUT 2: low hero angle on the colossal black mech-kaiju towering over the skyline as it rears back and unleashes a GIANT terrifying ROAR \u2014 jaws wide with fangs, red eyes and chest-core flaring blinding bright, blue lightning arcing off its head, the roar's shockwave rippling dust and rattling windows down the buildings, comic-style speed-lines and ink splatter bursting from the impact of the sound. It leans INTO the camera as the roar peaks. Hold on the roar."], "color": "#322", "bgcolor": "#533"}, {"id": 144, "type": "MarkdownNote", "pos": [-2085.5339999999997, 4871.944000000003], "size": [560, 900], "flags": {}, "order": 9, "mode": 0, "inputs": [], "outputs": [], "title": "HARD MODE - READ ME", "properties": {"Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"}, "widgets_values": ["# Hard mode - reference to video\n\nIdentity from **reference images, video and audio** instead of a start frame.\nUp to **9 images, 3 videos, 3 soundtracks, 3 standalone audios**.\n\n## The eviction node is ON, and should stay on\n\n`Evict text encoder` frees the ~16.5 GB text encoder once conditioning is computed,\nbefore the DiT loads. The encoder and the ~24 GB DiT do not co-fit in 32 GB, so\nwithout it the DiT loads partially and streams the remainder from system RAM on\nevery sampling step.\n\nMeasured on a 32 GB card, images only, `POST /free` before every run, runs\nalternated so machine drift could not fake the result:\n\n| eviction | time | output |\n|---|---|---|\n| bypassed | 4.5 min | identical |\n| **active** | **3.4 min** | identical |\n\n**24% faster, and bit-identical output** - every pairing scored 0.00 mean pixel\ndistance, motion 7.19 across all four runs. It costs nothing and changes nothing.\n\nWith a reference **video** the gap is far wider, because a reference video goes\nthrough the encoder's *vision* path: 6.5 min with eviction against a 46-minute\nrun that was killed without finishing.\n\nIf you ever disable it, use **Bypass**, never Mute. A muted node produces\nnothing, so the strength control loses its conditioning input and the graph\nstops validating.\n\n## Read this first: references and keyframes are MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE\n\nThis is a hard limit in ComfyUI's core, not a choice made here. `model_base.py`\nbuilds the conditioning payload like this:\n\n    if keyframes is not None:\n        payload[\"cond_video_latents\"] = [kf[\"latent\"] for kf in keyframes]\n    if refs is not None:\n        payload[\"cond_video_latents\"] = [r[\"latent\"] for r in refs ...]\n\nThe second is a plain **assignment**, so any keyframe latents are discarded\nwhile the keyframe *layout rows* survive - the sequence then desyncs and the\nsampler dies on a shape mismatch. There is no \"reference images + start frame\"\nmode, and forcing both does not degrade gracefully, it crashes.\n\nSo pick your tool per shot:\n\n| You want | Use |\n|---|---|\n| A specific opening/closing frame, or timed anchors | **H3_Keyframes.json** |\n| Identity carried by reference material | **this graph** |\n| 2-5 minute runtime | **H3_Multishot_MEMORY.json** |\n\n## Referring to your references in the prompt\n\nReference blocks are labelled in the prompt text and the numbering is\n**1-based**, while the input slots are **0-based**. So `ref_image_0` is\n`<Picture 1>`. Write prompts that name them:\n\n    <Picture 1> is the woman. <Picture 2> is the room she is standing in.\n    She walks to the window in the style of <Video 1>.\n\nOrdering is fixed by the node regardless of how you wire it: **all images, then\nvideos, then standalone audios**. A reference video WITH a soundtrack consumes\nan `<Audio j>` ordinal *before* your standalone clips - so one ref video with\nsound plus one `ref_audio_0` makes your voice clip `<Audio 2>`, not `<Audio 1>`.\n\nEmpty slots are skipped and numbering compacts, so leaving `ref_image_0` empty\nand filling `ref_image_1` still gives you `<Picture 1>`.\n\n## Reference audio must be STEREO\n\nThe audio VAE encodes `[B, 2, L]` and the layout reserves exactly two channels.\nA **mono** reference produces half the rows it reserved and dies deep in the\nmodel with no useful error. The stereo-guard node handles this - it forces\n2 channels at 32 kHz and trims length. Keep it wired.\n\n## Cost\n\nReference rows sit in the packed sequence on **every sampling step**, not just\nonce, so more references and a larger `ref_image_size` both cost time on every\nstep rather than once up front.\n\nMeasured, 124 frames at 480x864 with 2 reference images. These two runs were\ntaken back to back in a warm session, so the **ratio** is the trustworthy part\n- from a cold start both absolute figures are considerably higher:\n\n| setting | time | identity margin |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ref_image_size = match` | 2.9 min | +9.42 |\n| `ref_image_size = max` | 4.0 min | +9.10 |\n\nSo **1.38x**, not the \"several times slower\" that core's own tooltip warns about\n- and `max` did not improve identity here, scoring fractionally worse while\ncosting 38% more. It does change the output, so it is doing something; it just\ndid not buy identity fidelity at this resolution.\n\nCaveat: that margin is a blunt measure (distance to the reference images versus\ndistance to a control person the model never saw). It confirms identity carried,\nbut may be too coarse to see the fine facial fidelity `max` targets. At higher\noutput resolutions `max` is likelier to earn its cost. Start with `match` and\n2-3 images, and reach for `max` when you can see it help.\n\nReference audio, same test: about **14%** extra wall clock, and it trims motion\nroughly 17-27% - the audio conditioning constrains the performance rather than\nstalling it.\n\n## Reference video rules\n* minimum 5 frames, or it raises\n* silently truncated to the generation length, then trimmed to `n % 17 == 5`\n* shown to the encoder at 2 fps\n\n## Before you run this\n\nThe image slots default to ComfyUI's bundled `example.png` so the graph loads\nwithout missing-file errors -- **swap in your own reference images**, they are\nthe entire point of this mode.\n\nThe reference-audio branch (LoadAudio + the stereo guard) ships **muted**,\nbecause there is no example audio to point it at. Unmute both nodes and load a\nvoice clip to use it. It is optional: identity from images alone works, and the\naudio references cost extra time on every sampling step.\n"], "color": "#432", "bgcolor": "#653"}, {"id": 141, "type": "LoadAudio", "pos": [-1507.303000000001, 4675.95500000001], "size": [320, 136], "flags": {}, "order": 10, "mode": 2, "inputs": [], "outputs": [{"name": "AUDIO", "type": "AUDIO", "slot_index": 0, "links": [283]}], "title": "voice reference (optional)", "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.30.0", "Node name for S&R": "LoadAudio"}, "widgets_values": ["voice_reference.wav", null, null]}, {"id": 142, "type": "H3ReferenceAudio", "pos": [-1173.2400000000023, 4697.251000000016], "size": [330, 90], "flags": {}, "order": 15, "mode": 2, "inputs": [{"name": "audio", "type": "AUDIO", "link": 283}], "outputs": [{"name": "AUDIO", "type": "AUDIO", "slot_index": 0, "links": [284]}], "title": "stereo guard - MONO WILL CRASH", "properties": {"Node name for S&R": "H3ReferenceAudio"}, "widgets_values": [10], "color": "#232", "bgcolor": "#353"}, {"id": 136, "type": "MiniMaxH3ReferenceToVideo", "pos": [-772.0244563000001, 4976.602500000004], "size": [410, 530], "flags": {}, "order": 17, "mode": 0, "inputs": [{"name": "clip", "type": "CLIP", "link": 272}, {"name": "vae", "type": "VAE", "link": 273}, {"name": "audio_vae", "type": "VAE", "link": 274}, {"label": "ref_image_0", "name": "ref_images.ref_image_0", "shape": 7, "type": "IMAGE", "link": 278}, {"label": "ref_image_1", "name": "ref_images.ref_image_1", "shape": 7, "type": "IMAGE", "link": 282}, {"label": "ref_image_2", "name": "ref_images.ref_image_2", "shape": 7, "type": "IMAGE", "link": 290}, {"label": "ref_image_3", "name": "ref_images.ref_image_3", "shape": 7, "type": "IMAGE", "link": null}, {"label": "ref_video_0", "name": "ref_videos.ref_video_0", "shape": 7, "type": "IMAGE", "link": null}, {"label": "ref_video_audio_0", "name": "ref_video_audios.ref_video_audio_0", "shape": 7, "type": "AUDIO", "link": null}, {"label": "ref_audio_0", "name": "ref_audios.ref_audio_0", "shape": 7, "type": "AUDIO", "link": 284}, {"label": "ref_audio_1", "name": "ref_audios.ref_audio_1", "shape": 7, "type": "AUDIO", "link": null}, {"name": "prompt", "type": "STRING", "widget": {"name": "prompt"}, "link": 279}, {"name": "width", "type": "INT", "widget": {"name": "width"}, "link": 276}, {"name": "height", "type": "INT", "widget": {"name": "height"}, "link": 277}, {"name": "length", "type": "INT", "widget": {"name": "length"}, "link": 275}], "outputs": [{"name": "positive", "type": "CONDITIONING", "links": [288]}, {"name": "LATENT", "type": "LATENT", "links": [271]}], "title": "REFERENCE TO VIDEO - identity comes from here", "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.30.0", "Node name for S&R": "MiniMaxH3ReferenceToVideo"}, "widgets_values": ["", 1344, 768, 124, "match"]}, {"id": 143, "type": "H3ConditionStrength", "pos": [-734.9245562999998, 4846.851200000005], "size": [330, 90], "flags": 